{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.791,
   "text": "Every Thanksgiving, my grandmother set one extra plate at the end of the table."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.391,
   "end": 13.401,
   "text": "Nobody sat there. Nobody asked why. That was the rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.201,
   "end": 20.559,
   "text": "This year was our first Thanksgiving without her. My aunt called the extra plate silly... and put it away."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.259,
   "end": 25.461,
   "text": "We ate. We laughed. For a few hours, it almost felt normal."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 26.261,
   "end": 30.037,
   "text": "Then, just before midnight, the dining room went cold."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 30.737,
   "end": 34.748,
   "text": "Every candle on the table leaned... toward the empty end."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 35.348,
   "end": 38.719,
   "text": "And in the dark, a chair slid out by itself."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 39.619,
   "end": 41.475,
   "text": "Something sat down."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 44.075,
   "end": 50.603,
   "text": "Nobody moved. The only sound was a fork... tapping slowly on the bare wood where the plate should have been."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 51.403,
   "end": 58.059,
   "text": "My little cousin started to cry. So I filled a clean plate, and set it down in front of the empty chair."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.859,
   "end": 62.528,
   "text": "The tapping stopped. The candles stood straight again."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 63.928,
   "end": 67.021,
   "text": "In the morning, the plate was scraped clean."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 67.821,
   "end": 71.683,
   "text": "And under it was a note, in my grandmother's handwriting."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 73.283,
   "end": 76.568,
   "text": "Next year... set two plates. It's bringing me."
  }
 ],
